1 NAME Ichise /Chanyu of the Great Hunnic Empire/
2 GIVN Ichise
2 _MARNM Chanyu of the Great Hunnic Empire
1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biography: https://historica.fandom.com/wiki/Ichise_Chanyu#:~:text=Ichise%20Chanyu%20was%20the%20brother,Bi%20to%20flee%20to%20China.&text=Ichise%20died%20in%20114%20BC%20and%20was%20succeeded%20by%20Uwei%20Chanyu.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ichise Chanyu was the brother of Gunchen Chanyu and the son of Laoshang Chanyu, and he succeeded his brother as chanyu of the Xiongnu in 126 BC. He had to defeat the next-in-line to the throne, "the Wise Prince" Yui Bi, and he for
2 CONC ced Yui Bi to flee to China. Tens of thousands of Huns raided northern China in 126 BC, killing regional governor Gun Ji at Daigun and capturing 1,000 people; he also captured 1,000 people at Yaimin. In 125 BC, he led 30,000 Huns 
2 CONC on a raid into the Ordos, killing and capturing a multitude of officials and people at Shuofang. In 124 BC, Wei Qing led 100,000 Han cavalry to attack Shuofang, capturing 15,000 Huns while Ichise was drunk. Ichise responded with a
2 CONC nother raid, killing district chief Chu Yan and capturing 1,000 people. In 123 BC, Wei Qing led another campaign against the Huns, killing or capturing over 19,000 of them, but the Han suffered heavy losses. Ichise captured the tr
2 CONC eacherous Hun prince Zhao Xin in battle, but he made him his chief adviser and had him marry his sister. Shanyu decided to abandon the Ordos and move to the north of the Gobi Desert, forcing Chinese armies to march through the ste
2 CONC ppes, where they would be massacred. Ichise died in 114 BC and was succeeded by Uwei Chanyu.
