2 CONT Ching Kung of Yan (燕敬公) was a ruler of the State of Yan (燕国) during ancient China. He was estimated to have lived before 365 BCE and was the husband of N.N. of Yan and the father of Cheng Hou of Chao (成侯). His reign took place dur
2 CONC ing the Warring States period (475–221 BCE).
