1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_of_Yan
2 CONT
2 CONT Ping Kung of Yan (燕平公) was a ruler of the State of Yan (燕国) during ancient China. He was the son of Kung Kung of Yan and the father of Hsien Kung of Yan. His reign took place during the Warring States period (475–221 BCE), a time 
2 CONC of intense political and military conflict among various states.
2 CONT
2 CONT The State of Yan was one of the major states during this period, known for its strategic location and military campaigns.
