2 CONT Kung Kung of Yan (燕共公) was a ruler of the State of Yan (燕国) during ancient China. He was the son of Tao Kung of Yan (燕悼公) and the father of Ping Kung of Yan (燕平公). His reign took place during the Warring States period (475–221 BCE
2 CONC ), a time of intense political and military conflict among various states.
