1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Duke Lí of Zheng (鄭釐公), also known as Kūn Wán (髡頑) or Yùn (惲), was a ruler of the state of Zheng in ancient China. He lived during the late 6th century BCE, with his birth estimated around 590 BCE and his passing a
2 CONC round 566 BCE. He was the son of Duke Cheng of Zheng (鄭成公) and the father of Duke Jian of Zheng (鄭簡公) and Zǐ Shàn (子善).
2 CONT
2 CONT The state of Zheng was an influential feudal territory during the Zhou dynasty, known for its political maneuvering and regional conflicts.
