1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhuang_Bo_of_Quwo
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Zhuang of Quwo or Earl Zhuang of Quwo (Chinese: 曲沃莊伯; pinyin: Qūwò Zhuāng Bó), personal name Ji Shan, was a ruler of the Quwo (曲沃) state. He was the son of the founding ruler of Quwo, Huan Shu, and half-brother of Viscount W
2 CONC u of Han, the first leader of the Han clan.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 724 BC, Count Zhuang killed Marquis Xiao of Jin in the capital of Jin, Yi (翼). Then, Jin troops attacked Count Zhuang, forcing the latter to retreat to Quwo. Marquis E of Jin then ascended to the Jin throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Records of the Grand Historian, when Count Zhuang heard the news of the death of Marquis E of Jin, he led troops to attack Jin. King Huan of Zhou[1] ordered the Duke of Guo (虢公) to attack Count Zhuang, resulting i
2 CONC n Count Zhuang's retreat to Quwo. The Jin people then supported Marquis E of Jin's son, Marquis Ai of Jin, to take the throne of Jin.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Zuo Zhuan has a different record of the event. It says that Count Zhuang had an alliance with the Zheng and Xing (邢) states and they attacked the Jin capital, Yi. King Huan of Zhou sent troops to assist Count Zhuang. Marquis E
2 CONC  of Jin fled to Sui (随). Soon afterwards, Count Zhuang betrayed King Huan of Zhou and attacked him. King Huan of Zhou then sent the Duke of Guo during the autumn of that year to attack Quwo and placed Marquis Ai of Jin on the Jin 
2 CONC throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 716 BC, Count Zhuang died and was succeeded by his son, Duke Wu.
