2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Xiang of Qin (Chinese: 秦襄公; pinyin: Qín Xiāng Gōng; died 766 BC), personal name unknown, was a duke of the state of Qin, ruling from 777 BC to 766 BC. He was the first Qin ruler to be granted a noble rank by the king of the Z
2 CONC hou dynasty; under his reign, Qin was formally recognized as a major vassal state of the Zhou dynasty.[1][2]
