1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duke_Wu_of_Qi
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Wu of Qi (Chinese: 齊武公; pinyin: Qí Wǔ Gōng), personal name Lü Shou, was from 850 BC to 825 BC the duke of the Qi state.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Wu succeeded his father, Duke Xian, as ruler of Qi. He reigned for 26 years and died in 825 BC. He was succeeded by his son, Duke Li.[1][2]
