2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Gui of Qi (Chinese: 齊癸公; pinyin: Qí Guǐ Gōng), personal name Lü Cimu, was a duke of the Qi state.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Gui succeeded his father, Duke Yi, and was succeeded by one of his sons, Duke Ai.[1][2]
