1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gongbo
2 CONT
2 CONT Gongbo (Chinese: 公伯; pinyin: Gōngbó, died 845 BC), personal name unknown, was the third ruler of the state of Qin. Gongbo succeeded his father, the Marquis of Qin, who died in 848 BC, and ruled for three years. He died in 845 BC a
2 CONC nd was succeeded by his son Qin Zhong.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Although Qin would eventually develop into a major power that would conquer all other Chinese states and unite China proper to form the Qin dynasty in 221 BC, at the time of Gongbo it was still a minor state of the Western Zhou dy
2 CONC nasty and little is known about Gongbo.[2] 
